Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: smp2p: preserve edge history without a remote restart

qcom_smp2p_check_ssr() clears every inbound entry's last_value even when
RESTART_DONE has not changed. The next notification therefore presents
unchanged high bits as new rising edges. On Houji this repeatedly delivers
ADSP ready and handover interrupts during ordinary mailbox activity.

Return before clearing the edge history unless an SSR acknowledgement is
actually required. Keep the existing rescan after a real remote restart.
This fixes duplicate DSP notifications; it is not a claimed display fix.

The intended restart condition appeared in the earlier v2-support posting:
https://lkml.iu.edu/2509.3/00011.html
---
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c
@@ -194,6 +194,9 @@
 
 	restart_done = in->flags & BIT(SMP2P_FLAGS_RESTART_DONE_BIT);
 	restart = restart_done != smp2p->ssr_ack;
+	if (!restart)
+		return false;
+
 	list_for_each_entry(entry, &smp2p->inbound, node) {
 		if (!entry->value)
 			continue;
